 "known_caveats_not_fixed": [
  "The resting penetration scales as contact_dt^2 (the compliance acts at the velocity level), so halving contact_dt makes the floor four times stiffer, while MuJoCo's rest gap is dt-independent. Not addressed.",
  "At MuJoCo's own resting pose the model's total normal force is ~2.4x MuJoCo's, identically with the compliance enabled and disabled: the fix moves the equilibrium height, not the contact stiffness at a given penetration.",
  "12 ADMM iterations are not exact. Worst measured truncation with the compliance over a (band, gap) grid is 9.2e-3 relative (band 0.06, 10 mm penetration, two contacts at different partial gates) against 1.1e-2 relative for the legacy law at its own worst state on the same grid. Parity with the historical solver, not exactness.",
  "The compliance floor is derived from the constructor argument and is not persisted in the state_dict, exactly like contact_regularization and the gate band; loading a sidecar into a model built with a different contact_compliance changes the floor.",
  "c0 is one number per contact point and is only trainable where the gate is tapering; nothing here demonstrates that a real fit recovers a useful c0."
